# PRODUCT.md and DESIGN.md have to sit at the repo root for the tooling to
# resolve them, but this repo is also the deployed site. They hold strategy
# and internal state, not secrets - still nobody's business at a public URL.
#
# The trailing ! is required. Without it Netlify serves the real file and
# ignores the rule, because redirects only apply when no file matches.
/PRODUCT.md    /404.html  404!
/DESIGN.md     /404.html  404!
/og-card.html  /404.html  404!
